<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐποικ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go as settler</i> or <i>colonist to</i> a place,
				<i>settle in</i> a place, c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυκλάδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					1583
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βοιωτίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					9.2.25
				</span></i>
			 ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῇ Ἀσίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.2.10
				</span></i>
			 : abs., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				752e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be settled near</i> or <i>with hostile views against,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.86
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Δεκέλεια τῇ χώρᾳ
				ἐπῳκεῖτο</span> Decelea <i>was occupied as the seat of
				offensive operations against</i> their country, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.27
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
